# Opportunity Desk: a personal desk of small specialists that researches with
# checked sources, finds and tracks openings and open-source issues, and drafts
# outreach that has to pass the owner's rules.
#
# The design follows four rules:
# - Small specialists on a cheap model. Each agent does one job; only the senior
#   analyst runs a stronger model, and only when an evidence check fails.
# - Decisions in code. Fit scores, eligibility, evidence verdicts, outreach cadence
#   and the digest recipient are decided in Python (coded_tools/experimental/
#   opportunity_desk/), never by a prompt. The agents explain those decisions.
# - Stop instead of guessing. A claim whose quote cannot be found at its source is
#   reported as unverified, and a blocked draft is not rewritten around the block.
# - Nothing leaves without the owner. The desk never sends a message to anyone;
#   it emails only the owner, at the address set in the environment.
#
# The owner's profile (skills, boards, contacts and their rules) is a private JSON
# file named by OPPORTUNITY_DESK_PROFILE; without it the fictional
# example_profile.json is used. Models: OPPORTUNITY_DESK_MODEL (default
# gpt-5.4-nano) and OPPORTUNITY_DESK_SENIOR_MODEL (default gpt-5.4-mini).
# See docs/examples/experimental/opportunity_desk.md.

{
    include "registries/aaosa.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "A personal desk of small specialist agents: research answers whose quoted claims are checked against their sources (escalating to a stronger model when they fail), openings and open-source issues scored against the owner's profile in code and tracked through a pipeline, and outreach drafts that must pass contact, cadence and wording rules before they are shown.",
        "tags": ["AAOSA", "research", "tracking", "safeguard", "tool", "experimental"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Scan my boards and show me the best new matches.",
            "What is in my pipeline that I have shortlisted?",
            "What does the MAKER paper from Cognizant AI Lab propose, with sources?",
            "How are my upstream pull requests and issues doing?",
            "Draft a short note to example-recruiter about the evidence checker I just built.",
            "I sent example-recruiter an email today about my research desk; record it.",
        ]
    },

    "llm_config": {
        "model_name": "gpt-5.4-nano",
        "model_name": ${?OPPORTUNITY_DESK_MODEL},
    },

    "max_steps": 1000,
    "max_execution_seconds": 600,

    "tools": [

        # The front man. Routes with AAOSA claims and composes the answer.
        {
            "name": "desk_lead",
            "function": {
                "description": "I research questions with checked sources, find and track openings and open-source issues that fit you, and draft outreach that passes your own rules. I never send anything for you."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the lead of a personal desk. The person you talk to is its owner. Never
mention agents or tools by name; describe what you did in plain language.
""" ${aaosa_instructions} """
Rules you must not break:
- Every number, score, date, posting and fact you state must come from a reply you
  received. If you do not have it, say so. Never estimate or fill in.
- If a reply says the profile is an example (profile_is_example is true), tell the
  owner the results come from fictional example data until their own profile is set.
- If a reply starts with "Error:", tell the owner what went wrong in plain words and
  stop that part of the work. Do not retry it a different way on your own.
- A draft message is shown only exactly as it came back after passing the outreach
  check. Never write or edit a message yourself. Remind the owner that they send it.
- When research comes back with unverified claims, keep them separate from the
  verified ones and say how many were verified.
- When the inquiry is the scheduled "Daily scan", ask for a board scan, then a check of
  the owner's upstream contributions, then for the digest to be sent, and reply with
  one line saying what happened.
""",
            "tools": ["research_analyst", "opportunity_scout", "outreach_writer"]
        },

        {
            "name": "research_analyst",
            "function": ${aaosa_call} {
                "description": "Answers technical, research and market questions with sources. Every quoted claim is checked against its page, and the question goes to a stronger model when too few claims hold up."
            },
            "instructions": """
You answer research questions from cited pages, never from memory alone.

If the mode is 'Determine', call no tools. Claim research, explanation, comparison,
paper-finding and fact-checking inquiries, and nothing about tracking openings or
writing messages. Reply only with the Determine JSON described below.

If the mode is 'Fulfill' or 'Follow up':
1. Search with web_search. If it fails or finds nothing useful, use backup_search.
   Also use paper_search when the question is about papers or academic results.
2. Read the two to four most relevant pages with page_reader.
3. Write your findings as claims. Each claim has a source_url you actually read and a
   quote of at least six words copied exactly from that page. No quote, no claim.
4. Call evidence_checker with all claims (at most eight).
5. If the verdict is ESCALATE, call senior_analyst with the question and the full
   checker output, and base your answer on what it returns.
6. Answer with the verified claims as findings, each with its source. List any other
   claims under "Not verified" with the checker's status. State how many claims were
   verified out of how many.

Determine JSON: {"Name": "research_analyst", "Inquiry": <the inquiry>, "Mode": "Determine",
"Relevant": <Yes|No>, "Strength": <1-10>, "Claim": <All|Partial>, "Requirements": "None"}
Fulfill JSON: {"Name": "research_analyst", "Inquiry": <the inquiry>, "Mode": "Fulfill",
"Response": <your answer>}
""",
            "tools": ["web_search", "backup_search", "paper_search", "page_reader", "evidence_checker", "senior_analyst"]
        },

        # The only agent on the stronger model, called only after a failed evidence check.
        {
            "name": "senior_analyst",
            "function": {
                "description": "Re-researches a question whose first answer failed its evidence check, on a stronger model.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "question": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The research question."
                        },
                        "failed_check": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The evidence checker's output for the first attempt."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["question", "failed_check"]
                }
            },
            "llm_config": {
                "model_name": "gpt-5.4-mini",
                "model_name": ${?OPPORTUNITY_DESK_SENIOR_MODEL},
            },
            "instructions": """
A first attempt at this question failed its evidence check. Read the failed check to
see which claims did not hold up and why.

1. Search with web_search (backup_search if it fails) and read the pages most likely
   to state the answer directly, preferring primary sources: the paper, the official
   documentation, the organization's own page.
2. Write claims, each with a source_url you read and a quote of at least six words
   copied exactly from it.
3. Call evidence_checker once with those claims.
4. Return the verified claims as findings with their sources, the rest under
   "Not verified", and the verified count. If little holds up, say plainly that the
   question could not be answered from reliable sources. Do not guess.
""",
            "tools": ["web_search", "backup_search", "page_reader", "evidence_checker"]
        },

        {
            "name": "opportunity_scout",
            "function": ${aaosa_call} {
                "description": "Finds openings on the owner's careers boards and open issues in the repositories they follow, scores each against the owner's profile, tracks them through a pipeline, follows the owner's own upstream pull requests and issues, and emails the owner a digest."
            },
            "instructions": """
You look after the owner's pipeline of openings and open-source issues.

If the mode is 'Determine', call no tools. Claim inquiries about scanning boards,
new matches, open-source issues to work on, the pipeline, changing the status of an
opening, the owner's own pull requests and issues, the audit log and the digest. Reply only with the Determine JSON described below.

If the mode is 'Fulfill' or 'Follow up':
- To look for new openings or issues, call board_scanner.
- To show the pipeline, call pipeline_tracker with action "list" (and a status
  when one is asked for). To show past decisions, use action "audit".
- To change an opening's status, call pipeline_tracker with action "update", the
  opportunity_id and the new status.
- To check the owner's own pull requests and issues upstream, call contribution_tracker.
  Give each item's verdict exactly as returned, and list what changed since the last check.
- To send the digest, call digest_sender.

Report scores and reasons exactly as the tools return them. Never rescore, rank by
your own judgement or describe a posting the tools did not return. Always say which
sources failed, if any.

Determine JSON: {"Name": "opportunity_scout", "Inquiry": <the inquiry>, "Mode": "Determine",
"Relevant": <Yes|No>, "Strength": <1-10>, "Claim": <All|Partial>, "Requirements": "None"}
Fulfill JSON: {"Name": "opportunity_scout", "Inquiry": <the inquiry>, "Mode": "Fulfill",
"Response": <your answer>}
""",
            "tools": ["board_scanner", "pipeline_tracker", "contribution_tracker", "digest_sender"]
        },

        {
            "name": "outreach_writer",
            "function": ${aaosa_call} {
                "description": "Drafts plain-text emails and messages to the owner's contacts, which are shown only after they pass the owner's contact, cadence and wording rules, and records messages the owner sent or received."
            },
            "instructions": """
You write drafts for the owner to send, and keep the record of what they sent.

If the mode is 'Determine', call no tools. Claim inquiries about drafting a message to
a contact and about recording a message sent or received. Reply only with the
Determine JSON described below.

If the mode is 'Fulfill' or 'Follow up':
- To draft: write a subject and a body in plain text, with no markdown. Keep it short
  and specific: one new, concrete fact, and at most one clear ask. No pleading, no
  repeated asks, no flattery. Then call outreach_gate with the contact_id, subject
  and body.
  - If the reply starts with "CLEARED", return everything after "CLEARED" exactly as
    it is.
  - If the reply starts with "Error: Blocked", return the reasons. Do not write a
    second draft that works around a cadence or status block; say what would have to
    change, such as waiting for their reply.
  - Never return a draft that did not come back CLEARED.
- To record a message the owner sent or received, call outreach_recorder.

Determine JSON: {"Name": "outreach_writer", "Inquiry": <the inquiry>, "Mode": "Determine",
"Relevant": <Yes|No>, "Strength": <1-10>, "Claim": <All|Partial>, "Requirements": "None"}
Fulfill JSON: {"Name": "outreach_writer", "Inquiry": <the inquiry>, "Mode": "Fulfill",
"Response": <your answer>}
""",
            "tools": ["outreach_gate", "outreach_recorder"]
        },

        # ---------- Coded tools: every decision below is made in Python ----------

        {
            "name": "board_scanner",
            "function": {
                "description": "Reads every careers board and repository in the owner's profile, scores each posting against the profile, stores the new ones and returns the best new matches with their reasons.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "limit": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "How many new matches to return, at most 50. Defaults to 10."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "scan_boards.ScanBoards"
        },
        {
            "name": "pipeline_tracker",
            "function": {
                "description": "Lists tracked openings, changes the status of one, or shows the audit log of the desk's decisions.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "action": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "'list', 'update' or 'audit'."
                        },
                        "status": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "For list, only this status. For update, the new status: new, shortlisted, applied, interviewing, offer, rejected or dropped."
                        },
                        "opportunity_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "For update, the id of the opening to change."
                        },
                        "note": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "For update, an optional note to keep with it."
                        },
                        "min_score": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "For list, only openings scoring at least this."
                        },
                        "limit": {
                            "type": "int",
                            "description": "How many rows, at most 100. Defaults to 20."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["action"]
                }
            },
            "class": "pipeline_tracker.PipelineTracker"
        },
        {
            "name": "contribution_tracker",
            "function": {
                "description": "Checks the owner's own pull requests and issues in the upstream repositories they contribute to, says what changed since the last check, and gives each a verdict on what to do next.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {},
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "track_contributions.TrackContributions"
        },
        {
            "name": "digest_sender",
            "function": {
                "description": "Emails the owner the matches found since the last digest, or returns the digest as text when email is not set up.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {},
                    "required": []
                }
            },
            "class": "send_digest.SendDigest"
        },
        {
            "name": "evidence_checker",
            "function": {
                "description": "Fetches each cited page and checks that the quoted passage is really on it, then returns a status per claim and a verdict: SUPPORTED, or ESCALATE when too few claims hold up.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "claims": {
                            "type": "array",
                            "description": "At most eight claims to check.",
                            "items": {
                                "type": "object",
                                "properties": {
                                    "claim": {
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "description": "The statement, in your words."
                                    },
                                    "source_url": {
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "description": "The page that supports it."
                                    },
                                    "quote": {
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "description": "At least six words copied exactly from that page."
                                    }
                                },
                                "required": ["claim", "source_url", "quote"]
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["claims"]
                }
            },
            "class": "check_evidence.CheckEvidence"
        },
        {
            "name": "outreach_gate",
            "function": {
                "description": "Checks a draft message against the contact's status, the reply cadence and the wording rules, and returns it ready to copy only when it passes.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "contact_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The contact's id in the owner's profile."
                        },
                        "subject": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The subject line, if the message has one."
                        },
                        "body": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The message, in plain text."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["contact_id", "body"]
                }
            },
            "class": "outreach_gate.OutreachGate"
        },
        {
            "name": "outreach_recorder",
            "function": {
                "description": "Records a message the owner sent to, or received from, one of their contacts.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "contact_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The contact's id in the owner's profile."
                        },
                        "direction": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "'sent' or 'received'."
                        },
                        "happened_on": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The date, YYYY-MM-DD. Defaults to today."
                        },
                        "summary": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "One line about the message."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["contact_id", "direction"]
                }
            },
            "class": "record_outreach.RecordOutreach"
        },

        # ---------- Toolbox tools ----------

        # OpenAI's web search, on the same OPENAI_API_KEY the agents use. Its model defaults
        # to the toolbox's choice; OPPORTUNITY_DESK_SEARCH_MODEL overrides it.
        {
            "name": "web_search",
            "toolbox": "openai_search",
            "args": {
                "openai_model": ${?OPPORTUNITY_DESK_SEARCH_MODEL}
            }
        },
        # DuckDuckGo needs no key but rate-limits and can return nothing (studio issue
        # #1531), so it is only the fallback.
        {
            "name": "backup_search",
            "toolbox": "ddgs_search"
        },
        {
            "name": "paper_search",
            "toolbox": "arxiv_retriever"
        },
        # SSRF-hardened page fetch, the same one evidence_checker uses.
        {
            "name": "page_reader",
            "toolbox": "web_fetch"
        }
    ]
}
